  "version": 1,
  "title": "OEIS A364111: Bala's p^(3r) supercongruences",
  "abstract": "For integers A ≥ 2 and B, C ≥ 1 let u(N) = Σ_{k=0}^{N} C(N+k−1, k)^A C(2N−2k, N−k)^B C(2k, k)^C. The package proves that u(np^r) ≡ u(np^{r−1}) (mod p^{3r}) for every prime p ≥ 5 and all n, r ≥ 1, as conjectured by Peter Bala (OEIS A364111, 2023), and the case (A, B, C) = (2, 1, 1), which is A364111 itself. The proof uses Coster's method, as Osburn and Sahu did for the generalized Domb numbers.",
